#!/usr/bin/env node
// wal-conformance.mjs — 45-d concept-adopter (resumed) — WAL-EDL ADOPTION
// (SuperInstance/tessera seeds/wal-edl/wal-edl.ts).
//
// PROVENANCE: adopts the REPLAY SEMANTICS of tessera's wal-edl seed (a
// 350-line zero-dep typed append-only WAL whose EDL is fold(wal) and whose
// crash-safety is replay). The reference was OBSERVED LIVE by this lane —
// tools/wave45/45d-waledl-probe-receipt.json (generated by running tessera's
// seed under node; ranAt 2026-09-27T23:07:28Z, re-run byte-identical modulo
// timestamps) — and its semantics are re-expressed from scratch here. No
// shared code, no import of tessera (a conformance tester must not link the
// reference engine).
//
// THE CONFORMANCE QUESTION: do the fleet's stone-chain files verify like
// typed append-only WALs? Each chain is replayed as a WAL (records = rows;
// chained checksum = row_hash = SHA-256(canonicalJSON([prev, row]))) under
// torn-tail / corrupted-byte / full-chain scenarios, and the observed
// semantic class must match wal-edl's:
//   (a) TORN TAIL (last record cut mid-bytes): the good prefix verifies,
//       the tear is reported explicitly — reason shaped exactly like
//       wal-edl's: 'torn tail: N byte(s) after last newline' — plus
//       goodBytes, the recovery position (wal-edl's writer truncates there;
//       this tool is READ-ONLY and only receipts it).
//   (b) CORRUPTED BYTE (first / middle / last record): apply-nothing AT OR
//       PAST the break — the corrupted record and everything after it never
//       enter the fold (wal-edl: applied = firstBad seq - 1); report
//       'checksum mismatch at seq N'. Stone binds prev inside row_hash, so
//       wal-edl's separate 'chain break at seq N' class (explicit prev
//       mismatch) is exercised on the ported wal-edl WAL itself; disclosed.
//   (c) FULL CHAIN: replay clean, applied = all rows, tip/links match the
//       pins, deployed-path control (verify-fleet's pinned stone verifier,
//       offline) ok.
//
// SEMANTICS CHOSEN (documented; see tools/wave45/45d-conformance-claims.json):
//   recover-to-prefix, READ-ONLY. Default: any damage -> exit non-zero.
//   --torn-ok: exit 0 IFF damage is a torn tail ONLY and the good prefix
//   verified with the damage explicitly reported. Mid-chain corruption is
//   never exit-0. Framing is receipted per chain: JSONL recovers a prefix
//   byte-exactly; document framing (pong = one JSON array) is all-or-nothing.
//
// Zero dependencies, node:crypto only. Keys: none. Offline only.
//
// Usage:
//   node tools/wal-conformance.mjs                # full conformance matrix
//   node tools/wal-conformance.mjs --chains=qthe,pong   # subset
//   node tools/wal-conformance.mjs --json         # JSON only
//   node tools/wal-conformance.mjs --out=<file>   # also write the JSON verdict
//
// Exit 0 iff every scenario's expected semantic class holds.

